  "manual_review": [
    {
      "basis": "Two explicitly distinct product profiles; the USD200/USD0.50 proposition is an unvalidated scenario. The prior native receipt is not whole-company cost or revenue.",
      "id": "evidence_class",
      "result": "PASS"
    },
    {
      "basis": "Provider and customer partitions reproduce the prior audited components, including unsuccessful construction and required maintenance. Zero new surplus allocation does not remove these costs.",
      "id": "accounts",
      "result": "PASS"
    },
    {
      "basis": "Required startup beyond virtual capital is START_INFEASIBLE; no partial operation or borrowing is invented. Quoted requirements and unknown historical costs stay visible.",
      "id": "startup",
      "result": "PASS"
    },
    {
      "basis": "Promotion, prior-invoice collection, protected balances, mandatory cost, service, income/reserves and one discretionary action are ordered before calculation.",
      "id": "month_order",
      "result": "PASS"
    },
    {
      "basis": "Shutdown incurs the full obligation, pays available unrestricted cash and carries unpaid balance. Due collections repay obligations; no restart. Cash and incurred costs are distinct.",
      "id": "cash_obligations",
      "result": "PASS"
    },
    {
      "basis": "Working capital is k*(F+v*Nnext) and constrains new earmarking. Cash-backing shortfalls are reported. Tax reserve cannot decline or produce an invented refund.",
      "id": "reserves",
      "result": "PASS"
    },
    {
      "basis": "New earmark is bounded by recovered after-tax operating surplus minus lifetime allocations, and unrestricted cash. Initial capital and receivables do not qualify; spent plus idle earmarks cannot be reused.",
      "id": "earned_allocation",
      "result": "PASS"
    },
    {
      "basis": "Included labor consumes resource time without a second cash charge. Failed construction remains an expense; upkeep starts only on promotion and savings apply multiplicatively only to variable provider components.",
      "id": "construction",
      "result": "PASS"
    },
    {
      "basis": "Remaining uses are an explicit resource-only recurrence, not guaranteed cash feasibility. Capacity payback charges every added request but excludes final-month uncollected invoices.",
      "id": "forecasts",
      "result": "PASS"
    },
    {
      "basis": "Month12 Nnext=0; operating enterprises retain k*F, final invoices stay uncollected. Stopped enterprises have no forward operating WC or new investment; obligations remain.",
      "id": "terminal_boundary",
      "result": "PASS"
    },
    {
      "basis": "Matched human duration remains unknown; all frozen sensitivities remain. Same-served and full annual-demand comparisons include failed and unserved fallback, full traditional enablement once, and explicit handoff only for served failures.",
      "id": "human_comparator",
      "result": "PASS"
    },
    {
      "basis": "Traditional worker pool is explicitly480 minutes/day. Customer, worker and provider effort are separate; omitted provider quotas, rate limits and daily scheduling remain unvalidated. Hypothesis human fallback duration remains null.",
      "id": "capacity_scope",
      "result": "PASS"
    },
    {
      "basis": "The zero-reinvestment collected-cash diagnostic applies only to fraction0 paths; investing paths use separately labeled full combined cost including incurred construction, capacity, failed candidates and upkeep. Both hold the simulated cohort fixed and exclude final unpaid invoices from collected revenue. Customer price equality uses face invoices and full annual demand. No guaranteed repricing equilibrium is claimed.",
      "id": "break_even",
      "result": "PASS"
    },
    {
      "basis": "Manager USDC, Ascension AGIALPHA and Jobs-v0 success use distinct quote bases, integer precision and worker-only receipts. Realization is hypothetical/adverse with liquidity, gas and collateral separate.",
